  "id": "clinical-depression",
  "term": "clinical depression",
  "definition": "Clinical depression is a depressive disorder marked by a noticeable change in a person’s usual functioning over at least two weeks, with depressed mood or loss of interest or pleasure as a central feature. It can also involve changes in sleep, appetite or weight, energy, movement, concentration, self-worth, guilt, and thoughts of death or suicide.",
